# exclusive is a guard, so a value the parser cannot vouch for refuses the whole
# listing rather than reading as no. A guard that fails open stops guarding and
# says nothing.
run available
exit 3
file tasks/M2-01.md
	---
	id: M2-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: true
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: tasks/M2-01.md: exclusive must be yes or no, found: true
